# Build context for `a2a-agents/Dockerfile`, which is built from the workspace
# root (it needs every path-dep crate) and so would otherwise `COPY . .` the
# whole checkout — several GB of it, since `target/` and the vendored MCP SDK
# dwarf the source.
#
# That is not just slow: host build artifacts copied into the builder are for a
# different target triple, so they are dead weight cargo ignores and rebuilds.
#
# Patterns are written without trailing slashes. Docker matches these with Go's
# `filepath.Match` plus `**`, where a trailing slash does not reliably match a
# directory — `target/` silently excludes nothing.

# Host build artifacts — the big one.
target
**/target

# Version control and tooling state.
.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# The vendored upstream MCP SDK: a reference submodule, excluded from the cargo
# workspace, not part of any build, and by itself several GB once built.
a2a-mcp/rust-sdk

# The Terraform provider — a separate Go toolchain, unrelated to the agent image.
terraform-provider-a2aagent

# Local environment state. Secrets in particular must never reach a build
# context, where they would be readable in the resulting layers.
.env
.env.*
**/*.log

# Docker's own files (the Dockerfile is passed to the builder separately).
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
